abstract: >-
  An inductive graph deep learning and network analytics framework for municipal crime
  analysis. The system constructs a spatio-temporal graph connecting 30,000 incident events
  across Chicago via k-d tree spatial-temporal indexing, trains a 2-hop GraphSAGE model
  for multi-class crime categorization across 30 primary statutory types, extracts 64-dimensional
  latent embeddings, and implements an explainable multi-factor scoring engine identifying
  71,915 candidate investigative links alongside a self-contained local Gradio dashboard.
